  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMDP Lot 16: TA for Strengthening Climate Resilience Systems on Water Sanitation Hygiene (SCRS-WaSH)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project strengthens the climate resilient delivery systems in water, sanitation and hygeine (WASH) intervention areas. The technical assistance (TA) provided is amplifying the impact of the financial aid that has been provided to the Government of Ethiopia&#x2019;s (GoE&#x2019;s) One WaSH National Programme (OWNP).

The United Kingdom (UK) is the lead bilateral donor in the Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WaSH) sector in Ethiopia. Through this support, the UK assists the Climate Resilient pillar of the GoE&#x2019;s flagship programme, the One WaSH National Programme (OWNP) through the Strengthening Climate Resilience Systems in Water Sanitation Hygiene (SCRS-WaSH) programme (2019 &#x2013; 2024). The SCRS &#x2013; WaSH programme target CR WaSH regions, focusing on prioritised drought affected areas. Under the SCRS WaSH programme, Niras has been hired to implement the rural-focused Technical Assistance Project (TAP).

TAP provides support across five thematic areas; i) strengthening delivery systems of Climate Resilient (CR) WaSH services; transforming them into self-sustained delivery models, ii) establishing women and youth led systems for post construction maintenance management and spare part supply, iii) formulating a national WaSH Financing Strategy with emphasis on domestic resource mobilisation, iv) pilot innovative private sector supplies with emphasis on effective Menstrual Hygiene Management products at targeted programme schools, and v) Conduct adaptive learning evaluation through operational and adaptive research to improve programme delivery. In all these interventions climate resilience, gender and social inclusion are cross cutting themes that integrate through all activities.</narrative>
  </description>
